{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/798369-ideas-for-a-pantheon-purview-for-the-yozi","id":798369,"title":"Ideas for a Pantheon Purview for the Yozi","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-02T13:20:16-08:00","id":798369,"title":"Ideas for a Pantheon Purview for the Yozi","content":"So, for reasons I'm musing on a crossover between Scion and Exalted including a character that's a Scion of Ligier, but I'm having trouble deciding on a theme for a pantheon specific purview for them which isn't just cribbing off the transhumanism themes of the Infernal Exalted.<br /> <br /> As I see it, there's three big unique things with the yozi that could be woven into a pantheon specific purview;<br /> <br /> 1) Their eldtritch-ness (A green sun, a sea of poison, a silver desert stretching to infinity, etc and so on)<br /> 2) Their tendency to be locations (Demons that are also streets, forests, martial arts dojos and so on)<br /> 3) Their soul hierarchy (Third circle demons to the yozi, second circle to the third, even first circle if you go by the interpretation that they're basically the Yozi's dead skin flakes)<br /> <br /> Number 3 would be easiest to do. Maybe a power that has their birth rights be aspects of their souls and eventually at higher levels be able to make actual demons? 2 could probably go with that as well by having the location form be another aspect of their soul and switching between which one is their true form? One is harder to justify with that though. I suppose it could just be chalked up to flavor of the boons and birth rights without specifically being a mechanical thing? *shrug*<br /> <br /> Anyways, thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T04:40:34-08:00","id":800515,"title":"","content":"Well, the main hurdle i have with seeing it is that overall the Yozis are far more like <b>Titans</b> in their character and qualities than a pantheon of gods - though the Unshaped raksha from Exalted 1e &amp; 2e (and that apparently will be taken out - or at least not count as Raksha anymore - in Ex3) - look even more like Scion's titans and their avatars mechanically.<br /> <br /> Speaking of purview per se, the feeling i'm getting is one of Devil-Tiger charms converted in some sort of PSP from your description. It might be interesting but i'm kind of dubious on what would fit the lower, Hero level powers or how would the Yozis and the powers of their individualized souls fit into Scion's much more generalist frame.<br /> <br /> Power level-wise, i imagine one might adapt 2nd circle souls as demigod-level entities and 3rd circle demons as lesser deities (Legend 9-11). Blasphemy effects might be a sort of extreme form of Fateful Aura.<br /> <br /> Another thing that comes to mind is that you might check out chapter 4: Modern Age or even chapter 2: Heaven's Reach, from Shards of the Exalted Dream for extra ideas and alternate takes to mine for inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-04-2016, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}